# Ask for lesson diagram redraws from course sync

Matt asked (cc-matt-p, 2026-10-30) what code to paste to embed the redrawn
diagrams. None: since PR #593 the swap happens at render, keyed by Cloudinary
public id (`redrawForImage` in `src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx`), so his plain
markdown images already render as the code version. A new image shows as
itself until someone adds its redraw.

## Layer 1: detect (this task)

The applied course-sync Slack notice gets a `Not redrawn yet (n)` field
listing, per lesson, every Cloudinary image in the bodies the sync created or
updated that has no redraw and is not in `diagrams/not-drawings.ts`.

- `undrawnImages(body)` lives in `components/mdx/diagrams/index.tsx`, next to
  the registry it reads. Course sync only adds plan iteration
  (`course-sync/undrawn-images.ts`).
- Notice only. It never fails a sync, unlike `QuizQuestion` extraction.
- Retained resources are skipped, so an image is asked about when its lesson
  changes, not on every sync.
- `notDrawings` is the skip list for screenshots and photos. It starts empty;
  fill it from the first notices.
- `getCourseSyncPlanChanges` became `getCourseSyncPlan`: one plan read feeds
  both the narration and the redraw asks.

## Layer 2: redraw (proposed, not started)

Each flagged image starts a Claude Code cloud session (routine with an API
trigger, or `claude-code-action` via `repository_dispatch`) that adds the
redraw and opens a PR for review on the preview. Most new images are another
frame of a drawing already in code (`flows/frames.ts`). No auto-merge. Blocked
on infra: no Claude workflow in `.github/workflows`, no GitHub write token in
the app. Decide after layer 1 shows how many new drawings a sync brings.
